window.docContents[232].resolve({"/Tier-2___-definitions/Computational___Specifications___/Computational.Specifications.Session.SpkHop2Red/#file-Computational___Specifications___Session___SpkHop2Red":{"contents":"Paper › Computational/Specifications/Session › SpkHop2Red.leanTier 2 · definitions\n\nTier 2 · definitions used by the computational proof 2 headline theorems depend on it 56 of 139 lines trusted trust banner B3, trusted in part source ↗Read the definitions shown. Only the declarations that the headline statements use are shown, with the namespace, section, open and variable commands needed to read them. The collapsed runs are theorems, which Lean checks, and definitions that no headline statement uses.\n\nDeclarations on this page (8)def noBobCorrInEpoch0def noBobCorrWhileAliceBelowEpoch10def configRefuseEarlyBobCorrdef spkSwapHybridCountdef spkSwapSpuriousStepTermdef spkSwapCreationPointHitTermdef hop2CreateCollTermdef spkSwapHiddenScalarGuessTerm\n\nLeaked-pre-key game configuration and the terms of its hop 2Trusted in part. The theorems of Computational/Theorems/ use every definition in this file except KeyU, initKeysU and sessionSchemeU, which are checked by Lean; the ones they use are part of what you must read to trust the result. See Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md.The leaked-pre-key statement bounds the single-session SM game when Bob's signed-pre-key scalar s is fixed and known to the adversary (sessionSchemeFixedSpk), under early-corruption refusals configRefuseEarlyBobCorr (noBobCorrInEpoch0, noBobCorrWhileAliceBelowEpoch10). Its proof bridges to the uniform-start scheme sessionSchemeU in three hops: hop 1 replaces epoch-0 root-key derivation at Dh(s, T) by a PRF oracle; hop 2 couples known s with a uniform hidden scalar x by relabelling the random function on DhKerUniform fibers; hop 3 undoes hop 1 at x.Refusing corr-A (DEV-LS4) and corr-B (DEV-LS34) while epoch A < 10 keeps the first five round trips leak-free, so shared root keys form a single linear chain ρ₀, …, ρ₈ until Alice's fifth DH step evicts the epoch-0 receiver chain ck0 (maxReceiverChains = 5). In hop 2, replacing those spkSwapHybridCount = 9 root-KDF steps by random tables leaves spurious-step acceptance (spkSwapSpuriousStepTerm), honest creation-point hits (spkSwapCreationPointHitTerm), hybrid transition collisions (hop2CreateCollTerm), and s-world queries that hit the hidden public key pub x (spkSwapHiddenScalarGuessTerm).\n\n\n\n2 declarations not shown (lines 54–62): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesCryptoVerification.E2E.KeyU, CryptoVerification.E2E.initKeysU\n\ndef noBobCorrInEpoch0L64–70 ↗#DEV-LS33 (libsignal): no corruption of Bob in epoch 0. Refuses corr-B while epoch B = 0 (beyond configR1OnCurve, which refuses only Bob's epoch-0 sends, DEV-LS3). In libsignal's API, Bob's session exists only after his first successful decryption; earlier compromise exposes pre-key secrets handled at the PQXDH layer. Subsumed by noBobCorrWhileAliceBelowEpoch10 (DEV-LS34), since epoch B = 0 implies epoch A ≤ 1.\n\ndef noBobCorrWhileAliceBelowEpoch10L72–79 ↗#DEV-LS34 (formalization): no corruption of Bob while Alice is in epoch < 10. Refuses corr-B while epoch A < 10, as Bob's counterpart to DEV-LS4 (noAliceCorrWhileAliceBelowEpoch10). Effect: restricts the adversary; Bob compromises during the first five round trips (while Alice may still store the epoch-0 chain ck0) are excluded. With s known, corr-B in this window exposes Bob's root key and sending coins, and hence Alice's subsequent root keys, while ck0 remains reachable via pub s.\n\ndef configRefuseEarlyBobCorrL81–89 ↗#Session game configuration configR1OnCurve extended with noBobCorrInEpoch0 and noBobCorrWhileAliceBelowEpoch10 in corrOK.\n\n1 declaration not shown (lines 91–98): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesCryptoVerification.E2E.sessionSchemeU\n\nHop 2 bound terms\n\ndef spkSwapHybridCountL102–104 ↗#Number of root-KDF hybrids in hop 2 (ρ₀ through ρ₈, up to Alice's fifth DH step when ck0 is evicted).\n\ndef spkSwapSpuriousStepTermL106–114 ↗#Union bound over at most q spurious DH steps of Alice while she stores ck0, once all spkSwapHybridCount root-KDF tables are random. Each test evaluates expandPRG and the ideal acceptance probability of wireMacVerifiesTest, with supremum over chain counters c < 2 ^ 32 and wire lengths ser.length < 2 ^ 32 as in macForgeryProb (DEV-LS23).\n\ndef spkSwapCreationPointHitTermL116–120 ↗#Bound on the probability that a spurious DH output Dh.dh a T equals the honest creation point Dh.dh a (Dh.dh r Dh.base) over at most q + 1 receives of Bob with fresh scalar r.\n\ndef hop2CreateCollTermL122–129 ↗#Collision slack across the spkSwapHybridCount - 1 = 8 hybrid transitions k → k + 1 (table 0's creation entry is fixed before any query). Each transition budgets 6 * q fresh-scalar point-hit events: q against nonzero points already sampled lazily in table k + 1, and 5 * q against the at most 5 stored receiver-chain public keys (maxReceiverChains) per delivery.\n\ndef spkSwapHiddenScalarGuessTermL131–137 ↗#Bound on s-world divergence before hop 2's coupling breaks, when a query hits the independent hidden public key Dh.dh x Dh.base. Budgets 6 * q point-hit events: q deliver or inject sender ratchet keys and 5 * q stored receiver-chain keys (maxReceiverChains) while ck0 remains active.\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Computational/Specifications/Session/SpkHop2Red.lean","id":"/Tier-2___-definitions/Computational___Specifications___/Computational.Specifications.Session.SpkHop2Red/#file-Computational___Specifications___Session___SpkHop2Red"}});